      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The effect of cAMP phosphodiesterase inhibitor EG626 on the left ventricular function was studied in 23 patients with ischemic heart disease at rest and during the IHG test. Administration of a single dose of the substance produced changes in STIs indicating an increase in cardiac output and a possible enhancement of myocardial contractility during the IHG test. EG626 may have a beneficial effect on impaired left ventricular function in patients with ischemic heart disease."},
